------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project builds on jrystal, a JAX plane-wave DFT package:

    jrystal — https://github.com/sail-sg/jrystal
    Copyright 2025 Garena Online Private Limited
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

D3FT imports jrystal at runtime and does not redistribute its source. What it
uses from jrystal is the infrastructure: plane-wave basis and coefficients,
crystal and reciprocal-grid handling, FFT/braket helpers, kinetic and Hartree
operators, exchange-correlation, the spherical Bessel transform, configuration
and convergence utilities.

The norm-conserving pseudopotential path is NOT taken from jrystal. D3FT carries
its own implementation in d3ft/pseudopotential/, adapted from the corresponding
jrystal modules (pseudopotential.local, .nloc, .beta, .nlcc, .spherical) and
re-derived where those were incorrect for D3FT's purposes:

  * the Kleinman-Bylander term is conjugated on the inner projection, so an
    atom's projectors sit at +R rather than -R;
  * the local-potential radial quadrature keeps the [0, r_1] interval;
  * reciprocal-space norms and angles are NaN-safe under differentiation;
  * beta_l(|G+k|) is evaluated inside the JAX graph so gradients reach the cell.

d3ft/spectrum/ks_matvec.py likewise re-implements the Kohn-Sham
Hamiltonian-vector product in matrix-free form.

